On Thursday, June 14, 2012 3:44:43 AM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class="gmail_quote" style="margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex">Matt put his finger on why std::vector was slow
<br>compared to the current static allocations:
<br>
<br>     const int MAX_NODES = 1000000;
<br>     double adjoints[MAX_NODES];
<br>     int edges[MAX_NODES];
<br>
<br>If I change the above to use heap data, as in
<br>
<br>     double* adjoints = new double[MAX_NODES];
<br>     int* edges = new int[MAX_NODES];
<br>
<br>then the new auto-dif isn&#39;t any faster than the
<br>original one -- it might even be a bit slower.
<br></blockquote>
